  "readme": "Shared corpus proving the product invariant of PD-043: a saved TicketFilter selects the same set in apps/web (matchesFilter, in memory) and in apps/api (ticketFilterConditions, in SQL). Both suites read this file and assert the same expected ids, so a divergence fails a test instead of surfacing as a node that announces one number and lists another. Only fields the resolver already handles appear here; the five snapshot-derived ones are refused server-side and cannot be compared yet. A case may also carry a window (awake | sleeping | all), applied with today: the two tickets due on 09-02 and 09-03 sit on either side of the SLEEP_DAYS cut, so a side that moves the constant alone fails here. A day is a UTC calendar day, read off the ISO string: the ticket due at 01:30Z on 09-03 already sleeps.",
